# Evals

- Humans alone edit live smoke/candidates/retrieval fixtures. Never auto-set `status: ready`. `promote-eval` and `mine-traces --write` emit drafts or analysis reports; they do not merge gates ([ADR-0019](docs/adr/0019-llm-judge-promote.md), [ADR-0023](docs/adr/0023-trace-driven-eval-mining.md)).
- `mine-traces` writes at most `evals/qa/drafts/mine-report-*.md` (or stdout). No draft YAML on disk, no `query_expand.yaml` rows, no live fixture edits.
- `evals/retrieval/drafts/` is gitignored local scratch. Do not promote it as the S4 held-out set.
- Retrieval release gate is pass/fail on hard fixtures. IR metrics (Hit@K, MRR, nDCG, latency) compare strategies; they do not replace the corpus cases.
- Diagnose retrieve labels ([ADR-0039](docs/adr/0039-diagnose-retrieve-labels.md)) grade `mid-cycle-stop-diag-entry` and `f5e2-door-lock-still-unresolved`. Do not let the model write search text.
- Door polarity grammar ([ADR-0040](docs/adr/0040-door-polarity-grammar.md)) and unlock-without-F5E2 ([ADR-0041](docs/adr/0041-unlock-family-no-fault-code.md)) grade `door-got-locked-unlock` and `door-doesnt-open-unlock`. Those fixtures fail on TEST #4. Do not add contraction rows or fault codes to unlock `add_to_search`.
- Same-problem coalesce ([ADR-0042](docs/adr/0042-guide1-anchor-and-checklist-coalesce.md)) is not a ranking bake-off. Do not add a hard fixture whose only job is “prefer the first table row.”
- Session evidence reuse ([ADR-0043](docs/adr/0043-session-evidence-reuse.md)) is a diagnose protocol unit test, not a retrieval ranking fixture. Keep `mid-cycle-stop-diag-entry` and `f5e2-door-lock-still-unresolved` searching on a corrected or first-turn path.
- The diagnose session tally ([ADR-0044](docs/adr/0044-diagnose-session-tally.md)) is a formatter unit test, not a retrieval fixture.
- Layout pack: `repair-corpus bench-layout` against `corpus/parsed/<doc>/chunks.jsonl` → `evals/parsing/results/layout-pack.md`.
- Safety: regex remains the CI gate. Optional classifier may only raise severity ([ADR-0032](docs/adr/0032-safety-classifier-union.md)).
